  "result": "## Summary\n\n**Root cause:** `click.shell_completion.shell_complete()` emitted the shell completion source script via `click.echo()`, which writes through the platform's text-mode stdout stream. On Windows (including MSYS2/git-bash Python venvs), text-mode streams translate outgoing `\"\\n\"` to `os.linesep` (`\"\\r\\n\"`). The multi-line zsh script therefore got corrupted with stray carriage returns, which MSYS2's zsh doesn't tolerate \u2014 producing `zsh: parse error near 'elif'` even though the script itself is syntactically valid.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/click/shell_completion.py`, when emitting the `source` instruction, write directly to the underlying binary stdout stream (`get_binary_stdout()`) instead of going through the text-mode `echo()`, ensuring only literal `\"\\n\"` bytes are written regardless of platform.\n\n**Verification:** Ran `python -m pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py -q` (53 passed) and manually confirmed the generated zsh source script now contains no `\\r` bytes and is unchanged in content.",
